{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1785764229328,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"answer_id\":13,\"total_score\":5,\"scores\":{\"situation\":5,\"task\":0,\"action\":0,\"result\":0},\"strengths\":[],\"improvements\":[\"The candidate provided absolutely no context. This response is insufficient to evaluate the question.\",\"To provide a helpful evaluation, the candidate needs to describe *any* situation where they took initiative, even if it was small. They need to begin by explaining the project or task they were involved in.\"],\"feedback\":\"This answer demonstrates a significant gap in communication and preparation. The interviewer needs to understand *what* the candidate is referring to before any evaluation can be made. Please expand on your response and provide details about a situation where you took initiative.”, 1}”\",\"suggested_answer\":\"I understand this was a challenging start to our conversation. Let’s try a different approach. Can you tell me about *any* time you felt compelled to go above and beyond what was expected of you on a task or project? It doesn't have to be a huge accomplishment – even a small step outside your defined role is valuable information.\"}"]}
